Falsifies `jh7110_entropy::verification::an_unseeded_core_never_yields_bytes`.

The defect: `interpret` lets a standing `RAND_RDY` latch excuse a clear `STAT.SEEDED`. The latch is
write-1-to-clear and can survive from before the last reset, which is the case the `stat`
parameter exists to rule out; trusting it brings back "serve the contents of a register file
nobody seeded".

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(interpret(stat, istat, rand), Outcome::Unseeded)`: an unseeded core with
`RAND_RDY` latched returns `Ready`.

